course: dictionary
lesson: 2174
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Corridor is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask what would make sense there.
explain: «Rules like "walk, don't run" exist so people don't crash into each other in corridors.» People walk along corridors and crash into each other in them, so a corridor must be a passage inside a building.
explain: A wildlife corridor is a different kind of corridor. It is a long, narrow strip of land or air that lets animals move safely from one place to another. When you meet a word with two meanings, try each one in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
fact: A corridor is a long passage in a building with doors to rooms.
fact: A corridor can also be a long, narrow strip of land or air, like a wildlife corridor.
fact: Corridors are fire escape routes, so they must always stay clear.
fact: «Down the corridor» and «at the end of the corridor» tell you where something is along a passage.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so check the words around them before you decide.
exercise: «Rules like "walk, don't run" exist so people don't crash into each other in corridors.» What is a corridor in this sentence? | A strip of sky for birds | A wild animal's home | *A long passage in a building with doors to rooms | A kind of running race
exercise: A wildlife corridor lets animals move safely. What does corridor mean here? | A dark cave under the ground | A school rule about walking | *A long, narrow strip of land or air | A room with a door
exercise: Why must corridors always stay clear? | Because they are good places for playing games | Because nobody is allowed to walk in them | *Because they are fire escape routes | Because they are where teachers keep their lunch
test: «Once, when nobody's looking, Jake does their old secret handshake in the corridor.» Where does Jake do the handshake? | In the middle of a field | Under the sea | *In a long passage inside a building | On top of a hill in the sun
test: Lena walked down the ___ to find her classroom. | nest | cloud | *corridor | puddle
exam: Corridor can be a passage in a building or a strip of land or air. Which sentence uses the second meaning? | Jake did a secret handshake in the corridor | Wait at the end of the corridor for your friend | Walk, don't run in the corridor | *Wildlife corridors help animals travel safely
